#: ../../.opencode/commands/blocked.md:4
msgid ""
"Surface every open Feature whose progress is blocked. Two kinds of "
"blockers are joined automatically:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/blocked.md:7
msgid ""
"**Dependency-blocked** — Features whose `depends_on` / `blocks` edges "
"point at specs not yet `completed` / `accepted`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/blocked.md:9
msgid ""
"**AC-blocked** — Features whose Criterion nodes are `failing` or "
"`regressed`. (Phase-3 of `acceptance-criteria-graph` flips status from "
"run-result ingest, so this surfaces real test/AC failures.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/blocked.md:13
msgid "Run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/blocked.md:15
msgid "hero blocked\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/blocked.md:17
msgid ""
"The output is a tree of open features with their blockers underneath. "
"Surface it verbatim, then call out the most actionable item — usually the"
" deepest leaf (a failing AC, an upstream spec still in `planning`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/blocked.md:21
msgid ""
"If the user asks \"what's stuck on me?\", filter mentally by `claimed_by`"
" from `hero status` first, then route here."
msgstr ""

